  "notes": "ケチる is a casual verb derived from ケチ (stingy, cheap). It takes a direct object indicating what one is being stingy about.\n\nConjugation (godan):\n- ケチらない (negative)\n- ケチって (te-form)\n- ケチった (past)\n\nRelated words:\n- ケチ (noun/na-adjective: stingy person, stinginess)\n- ⟦ドケチ→ドケチ：09432_dokechi⟧ (super stingy - intensified)\n- ⟦けち→けち：02792_kechi⟧くさい (having a stingy manner)\n\nUsage note: Often used critically or self-deprecatingly. Using this about others can be insulting.",
